# pipeOS is offline-only: boot-time apk runs from the initramfs BEFORE
# networking is up, so a network repo here costs a resolver/connect timeout on
# every boot — and installs can silently resolve a newer network version whose
# .apk is not on the media, vanishing on the next reboot.
#
# To install something new, seed the local mirror instead (one-shot, network
# used explicitly): extra-add [--repo main|community] <pkg>...
# or by hand:
#   mount -o remount,rw /media/usb
#   apk fetch --recursive --arch x86_64 -o /media/usb/apks/extra/x86_64 \
#     --repository https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.24/main <pkg> <deps>
#   (re-index + sign the extra repo, then apk add <pkg>; lbu commit)
#   mount -o remount,ro /media/usb
#
# apks/dev: rollback-safe staging for locally built packages (pipeOS#8). Listed
# after apks/pipeos so a local rebuild's higher pkgver wins without ever
# writing to the known-good pipeos repo; `dev-push`/`dev-push --remove` manage
# it. apk always resolves the highest pkgver regardless of repo order, so this
# ordering documents intent rather than changing resolution.
/media/usb/apks
/media/usb/apks/pipeos
/media/usb/apks/dev
/media/usb/apks/extra
